							<h3>When Synthetic Data Hurts: DCGAN Augmentation Failure Under Extreme Data Scarcity for Cassava Disease Classification in East Africa</h3>
							<p class="authors">Patrick Ndowo, <strong>Innocent Nyalala</strong></p>
							<p class="venue">
								<a href="https://www.datascienceafrica.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DSA 2026 Workshop</a>, Makerere University, Kampala, Uganda (23–24 July 2026)
							</p>
							<p class="abstract">
								Investigates failure modes of DCGAN-based data augmentation under extreme data scarcity in cassava disease classification, revealing conditions under which synthetic augmentation degrades model performance in East African field settings.
							</p>
